# Vague Language Check

Detects vague language in user stories, requirements, technical specifications, and code comments. Prompts for more precise wording. Flags words like "quickly", "easily", "somehow", "maybe", "possibly" that lack specificity.

## When to Apply

Apply this rule when:
- Writing user stories
- Creating requirements
- Defining acceptance criteria
- Writing technical specifications
- Creating code comments (TODO/FIXME)
- Writing documentation that defines behavior
- Need precise, specific language
